            <ArticleTitle>Sigmoid colon perforation: result of accidental swallowing of a toothpick.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>535-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute surgical abdomen is a very serious situation that arises in various medical conditions. Common among them are appendicitis, foreign-body ingestion, and intestinal obstruction or perforation. These complications usually require emergency abdominal surgery. A case of rectal bleeding accompanied by acute surgical abdomen following the accidental ingestion of a toothpick is described in this report.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
